From: Jonathan Barnes <hello@jonbarnes.dev>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 11:46:48 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] A glow drawn over everything is not lit

Patch 0028 of the renderer series (OoT: Recompiled).

Navi's core, the bluish white body between her wings, is two quads of a glow texture that the
game draws with G_RM_CLD_SURF2 when the fairy is Navi: no depth test, no depth write, blended
over the framebuffer. Every other fairy uses the depth tested form, which is in the translucent
z mode and is already kept out of the traced scene. Navi's form is in the solid z mode, so the
sorting never saw it as translucent: it went into the traced scene and into the raster before
the composite, and was multiplied by the shadow of whatever surface stood behind it. In the
sun's shade her body dimmed and read as see-through, which the user reported on 2026-10-08 as
"her light disappears around the actual light body".

A draw that neither tests nor writes depth and reads the framebuffer to blend is an overlay laid
on the picture, not a surface in it. It now takes the translucent mask, so it is drawn after the
composite in its own color and alpha and traced by nothing. The game's choice of no depth test
is kept, so she still shows through a wall as she does on the console. An inventory of every room
in the game found no depthless draw, so the rule reaches only actors and effects drawn that way.

Rung 36 puts the old sorting back for a side by side, and takes the cut-out quads of patch 0027
like the default, so it differs from Off only in this.

diff --git a/src/render/rt64_framebuffer_renderer.cpp b/src/render/rt64_framebuffer_renderer.cpp
--- a/src/render/rt64_framebuffer_renderer.cpp
+++ b/src/render/rt64_framebuffer_renderer.cpp
@@ -1981,13 +1981,29 @@ namespace RT64 {
                         // 0027): Off, the unrelated shader experiments 1 to 7, 25 (the rule that
                         // won, which IS the default) and 30 to 34. The ladder's own historical
                         // rules (8 to 24, 26 to 29) and 35 keep exactly what they did.
-                        const bool defaultFamily = (cutoutRule < 8) || (cutoutRule == 25) || ((cutoutRule >= 30) && (cutoutRule <= 34));
+                        const bool defaultFamily = (cutoutRule < 8) || (cutoutRule == 25) || ((cutoutRule >= 30) && (cutoutRule <= 34)) ||
+                                                   (cutoutRule == 36);
                         if (defaultFamily && cutoutQuad) {
                             solidDraw = true;
                         }
+                        // A BLENDED DRAW WITH NO DEPTH AT ALL IS AN OVERLAY (patch 0028). It
+                        // neither tests nor writes depth and reads the framebuffer to blend, so
+                        // it is a glow laid over the picture, not a surface in it. It is not in
+                        // the translucent z mode, though, so the rule above never saw it: it
+                        // went into the traced scene and the raster before the composite, where
+                        // it was multiplied by the shadow of whatever stood BEHIND it. Navi is
+                        // the one this game draws that way (her core, two quads of a glow
+                        // texture under G_RM_CLD_SURF2; every other fairy uses the depth tested
+                        // form), so in the sun's shade her body dimmed and read as see-through
+                        // (the user, 2026-10-08: "her light disappears around the actual light
+                        // body"). As an overlay it takes the translucent mask: after the
+                        // composite, in its own color and alpha, traced by nothing. No room
+                        // draw in the game is depthless. Rung 36 puts the old sorting back.
+                        const bool depthlessOverlay = !otherMode.zCmp() && !otherMode.zUpd() && ((otherMode.L & IM_RD) != 0) &&
+                                                      otherMode.forceBlend() && (cutoutRule != 36);
                         // A translucent draw (the XLU z mode) gets a mask no ray carries (patch 0006).
                         const bool wasTranslucent = (otherMode.zMode() == ZMODE_XLU);
-                        if (wasTranslucent && !solidDraw) {
+                        if ((wasTranslucent && !solidDraw) || depthlessOverlay) {
                             raytracing.queryMask = TranslucentRayQueryMask;
                         }
                         else if (wasTranslucent && castsNothing) {
